      "section": "Tissue spots",
      "order": 3,
      "alignment": "left",
      "vertical_alignment": "top",
      "body": "Colonic glands stained for FHL2 (brown, DAB) with a hematoxylin counterstain (blue), overlaid with spots laid out like a Visium slide. Clusters group spots by their stain intensities, so C1 sits on the most DAB-positive tissue. The three gene counts are synthetic: gene_A follows DAB, gene_B follows hematoxylin, gene_C a left-to-right gradient. Pick clusters on the left, or lasso a region of the tissue.\n",
      "wf_tag": "python/bioimage_demo"
    },
